---
const updated = "September 2026";
---

<dialog
  id="privacy-dialog"
  tabindex="-1"
  class="bg-surface backdrop:bg-ink/60 m-auto w-[min(34rem,calc(100vw-2rem))] p-0 text-base outline-none"
  aria-labelledby="privacy-title"
>
  <div class="max-h-[85vh] overflow-y-auto p-8">
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
      <h2 id="privacy-title" class="text-3xl">Terms &amp; Privacy</h2>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-privacy-close
        aria-label="Close"
        class="text-muted hover:text-ink -mt-1 cursor-pointer text-3xl leading-none"
      >
        &times;
      </button>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4">
      This is a recipe site. It doesn't ask for your name, your email, or anything else about you.
      Here's the full picture of what happens when you visit.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl">Terms of use</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      The recipe and cooking tips are provided for general information. Check ingredients for
      allergens and follow food-safety guidance when preparing and storing food.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl">Analytics</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      We use <a href="https://usefathom.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
        >Fathom Analytics</a
      >
      to understand how people use this site. It counts page views and clicks on the navigation, recipe
      links, and this notice, and provides aggregate statistics such as referring sites, country, and
      browser type. Fathom does not use tracking cookies or build advertising profiles across websites.
      It briefly processes request information, including your IP address and user-agent, to create site-specific
      visitor signatures and produce these statistics.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Read more in Fathom's <a
        href="https://usefathom.com/legal/dpa"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        target="_blank">data processing agreement</a
      > and <a href="https://usefathom.com/data" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
        >data journey</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl">Fonts</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      The site loads typefaces from Google Fonts. To deliver them, your browser connects to Google's
      servers, which means your IP address is shared with Google as part of that request.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl">That's it</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">
      This site has no accounts or advertising, and we don't sell visitor data. The services
      described above receive the information needed to provide analytics and fonts.
    </p>

    <p class="text-muted mt-6 text-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-6 text-right">
      <button
        type="button"
        data-privacy-close
        class="bg-accent inline-block cursor-pointer px-5 py-3 text-sm tracking-[0.12em] text-white uppercase"
      >
        Close
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>

<script>
  const dialog = document.getElementById("privacy-dialog") as HTMLDialogElement | null;
  if (dialog) {
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-privacy-open]").forEach((el) =>
      el.addEventListener("click", () => {
        dialog.showModal();
        // showModal() autofocuses the first button (the ×); move focus to the
        // dialog itself so nothing shows a focus ring on open.
        dialog.focus();
      }),
    );
    dialog
      .querySelectorAll("[data-privacy-close]")
      .forEach((el) => el.addEventListener("click", () => dialog.close()));
    dialog.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
      if (e.target === dialog) dialog.close();
    });
  }
</script>
